# B0: the BUILD-ONLY job of the window, run BEFORE A0 while production still serves. C2_ACTIONS=build opens no card, resets nothing and stops nothing: it makes
# the one image of the window (the thin tt-vllm layer over the P8 base, with draft_wide_tp, the profiler hook and the traced-publication changes) from the pushed
# tp4/next-3 commit the window sits on. Without it every card job below would fail at its docker run and the window's stop job would halt with production already down.
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH. The build step skips a tag that already exists on the host, so a reused tag would silently serve an old image: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3m is a
# PLACEHOLDER and the driver substitutes ONE new tag, never used before, in every template of this window (and of the scope window, which shares the image) after
# checking the tag is absent from the host's images. A later commit needs a new tag again.
# Pass: the build log ends with the image tagged, the closure and provenance checks of the build pass. Stop rule: any failure stops the window before production is touched.
# Duration (estimate): 18 min typical, 90 at worst (the first build after a base change).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-3 windows (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
